by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-04T08:48:42Z

Thanks for folding this into `debug:messenger`, and for doing the extraction as well.

I checked the routing against a real container before touching anything: eleven message classes through `--message`, then the same classes through `dispatch()` against in-memory transports, in two configurations, one with a `*` route and one without. Every comparison matched, including the namespace wildcard beating `*`, configuration beating `#[AsMessage]`, and an attribute inherited from a parent class.

I rebased, squashed the twelve commits into one (one of them removed a command another one added), and fixed three things:

* `registerDebugCommandRouting()` keyed the attribute map by service id instead of by class. A message class registered under an id of its own, such as `app.my_message: {class: App\Message\Foo}`, made the whole command die with `TypeError: Unsupported operand types: array + bool`, because `class_parents('app.my_message')` returns `false`. `registerTypeMapping()` just above already resolves the class, so this now does the same.
* The per-message rules came from that same compile-time map, so an `#[AsMessage]` class that is not a registered service, one in an excluded path or in a library, printed `routed to audit` and then `No routing rules apply to this message.` The per-message view resolves the attributes by reflection now. The map stays for the global listing, which is the only place that has to enumerate attribute-routed messages.
* `--message='\App\Message\Foo'` answered `not handled` and `not routed`. `class_exists()` accepts the leading backslash but the senders map is not keyed with it, so the value is trimmed now.

Each of those has a test that fails without its fix. I also dropped a duplicate blank line after the `[INFO]` block.

Two smaller notes for the record. `$attribute->serializedTypeName ?? null` is not cosmetic: that property landed in 8.1 and FrameworkBundle allows `symfony/messenger ^7.4.10`, so the current code reads an undefined property there. And moving to `addResourceTag()` changes the autowiring error text from `excluded because it's a messenger message` to `excluded by tag "messenger.message"`, which is what `form.data_class` and `object_mapper.map` already produce.

The description is rewritten as documentation and ends with the points a symfony-docs pull request should carry. A documentation pull request is still needed.
